From: Vividh Yadav <vividh50@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:56:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep search-graph edges to duplicates whose distance rounds
 below zero

For some vectors, rounding gives alternative_dot a distance of about
-1.7e-7 between identical rows. The search graph is built as a
scipy-maximum union, which drops an edge present in one direction only
unless its distance is positive, and only exact zeros were raised to
FLOAT32_EPS beforehand. Such edges were dropped, and most copies of a
duplicated vector were left with no incoming edge: a query for the vector
found 74 of 200 copies. Raise all non-positive distances to FLOAT32_EPS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017uaXZrSYSh1iMaFrDMbm4o
---
 pynndescent/graph_utils.py             |  5 +++--
 pynndescent/pynndescent_.py            |  7 +++++--
 pynndescent/tests/test_pynndescent_.py | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/pynndescent/graph_utils.py b/pynndescent/graph_utils.py
index 40e8270..6431ae7 100644
--- a/pynndescent/graph_utils.py
+++ b/pynndescent/graph_utils.py
@@ -170,8 +170,9 @@ def adjacency_matrix_representation(neighbor_indices, neighbor_distances):
         (neighbor_indices.shape[0], neighbor_indices.shape[0]), dtype=np.float32
     )
 
-    # Preserve any distance 0 points
-    neighbor_distances[neighbor_distances == 0.0] = FLOAT32_EPS
+    # Preserve any distance 0 points, and the slightly negative distances rounding
+    # can give identical points
+    neighbor_distances[neighbor_distances <= 0.0] = FLOAT32_EPS
 
     result.row = np.repeat(
         np.arange(neighbor_indices.shape[0], dtype=np.int32), neighbor_indices.shape[1]
diff --git a/pynndescent/pynndescent_.py b/pynndescent/pynndescent_.py
index 822cd75..36a008d 100755
--- a/pynndescent/pynndescent_.py
+++ b/pynndescent/pynndescent_.py
@@ -1638,8 +1638,11 @@ class NNDescent:
                         self.diversify_prob,
                     )
 
-        # Preserve any distance 0 points
-        diversified_data[diversified_data == 0.0] = FLOAT32_EPS
+        # Preserve any distance 0 points. Rounding can also leave the distance
+        # between identical points just below zero (alternative_dot gives about
+        # -1.7e-7 for some vectors), and the union below drops an edge present in
+        # one direction only unless its distance is positive.
+        diversified_data[diversified_data <= 0.0] = FLOAT32_EPS
 
         # Union of forward and reverse edges, without self loops, degree pruned.
         # (The forward rows are already diversified; a further "reverse"
